// ASCII - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# ASCII is not really a binary format: it is the one every other
# encoding on the previous page is measured against. "Hello World!"
# is 12 bytes, all below 0x80, all printable.
0000  48 65 6C 6C 6F 20 57 6F 72 6C 64 21             |Hello World!|
